#### Example 1: Schema Deployment Pipeline

**Context**: Automated schema deployment for a multi-environment Kafka platform with backward compatibility validation

**Implementation**:

**Repository Structure**:
```
schemas/
├── avro/
│   ├── user-schema.avsc
│   ├── order-schema.avsc
│   └── payment-schema.avsc
├── json/
│   └── metadata-schema.json
└── scripts/
    ├── deploy-schemas.sh
    └── validate-compatibility.sh
```

**Jenkins Pipeline**:
```groovy
pipeline {
    agent any

    parameters {
        choice(name: 'ENVIRONMENT', choices: ['dev', 'qa', 'prod'])
        booleanParam(name: 'FORCE_DEPLOY', defaultValue: false,
                    description: 'Skip compatibility check')
    }

    environment {
        LENSES_TOKEN = credentials("lenses-${params.ENVIRONMENT}-token")
        LENSES_URL = "https://lenses-${params.ENVIRONMENT}.company.com"
    }

    stages {
        stage('Validate Schema Syntax') {
            steps {
                script {
                    def schemas = findFiles(glob: 'schemas/avro/*.avsc')
                    schemas.each { schema ->
                        sh "avro-tools compile schema ${schema.path} /tmp"
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Check Compatibility') {
            when {
                expression { params.FORCE_DEPLOY == false }
            }
            steps {
                script {
                    sh './scripts/validate-compatibility.sh ${ENVIRONMENT}'
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy Schemas') {
            steps {
                script {
                    sh './scripts/deploy-schemas.sh ${ENVIRONMENT}'
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Verify Deployment') {
            steps {
                script {
                    def schemas = ['user-value', 'order-value', 'payment-value']
                    schemas.each { subject ->
                        sh """
                            lenses-cli schema get \
                                --subject ${subject} \
                                --url ${LENSES_URL} \
                                --token ${LENSES_TOKEN}
                        """
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        success {
            slackSend(
                color: 'good',
                message: "Schema deployment to ${params.ENVIRONMENT} successful"
            )
        }
        failure {
            slackSend(
                color: 'danger',
                message: "Schema deployment to ${params.ENVIRONMENT} failed"
            )
        }
    }
}
```

**Compliance Evidence**:
- All schemas version-controlled in Git
- Backward compatibility verified before production deployment
- Automated validation prevents manual errors
- Audit trail via Jenkins build logs

**Lessons Learned**:
- Always validate compatibility in non-production first
- Use semantic versioning for schema versions
- Document breaking changes in commit messages
- Maintain schema evolution guidelines document

